decryption or signing 

Hash Functions - An Algorithm that transform a variable length input into a unique, fixed length output 
(one-way functions, cant be reversed) 

(MDS) Message Digest Algorithm 5 - Hashing function that converts data of any size into a fixed 128-bit digital figerprint 

(SHA-1) Secure Hash Algorithm - Hashing function that takes an input and produces a fixed 160-bit message digest

(SHA-2) Produces 224, 256, 384, and 512 bits

(SHA-3) Converts any digital input 

(RIPEMD) Produces 128, 160, 256, and 320-bits

(HMAC) Hash Based Message Authentication Code - Combines symmetric cryptography and hashing to provide authentication
