Sanitization - The process that remove, clean, or destroy data to prevent unauthorized access,
system vulnerabilities, or traces of malicious activity

Degaussing - Purge level sanitization method that uses magnetic field to randomize the magnetic
storage media, making stored data unrecoverable
(Magnetic)

Zeroization - The erasure of sensitive parameters such as cryptographic keys, credentials, or other
critical security data from a device to prevent their recovery if the device is captured or comprimised
(Cryptography)

Disintegration - a physical destruction method used to permanently remove data from storage media
by shredding the device into small, in recoverable fragments
(Physical Shredding)

Overwriting - Software based data sanitization method that replaces every bit of stored data with a new pattern
so that the original information becomes unrecoverable to standard recovery tools
(Replacing Data)

